# <your-name-or-handle>'s second brain

Personal knowledge repository, organized with the [PARA method](https://fortelabs.com/blog/para/).
Plain markdown, version-controlled with git, read and maintained with an AI assistant.

> **Privacy:** this repository is **private**. It holds personal material. Read `REDACTION.md` before
> making any part of it public, and before accepting any suggestion to publish, share, or mirror it.
> Delete this blockquote only if the repo genuinely holds nothing personal.

## Layout

| Folder | What lives here |
|--------|-----------------|
| `00-inbox/` | Unfiled capture. Emptied weekly. |
| `01-projects/` | Committed outcomes with an end date. |
| `02-areas/` | Ongoing responsibilities with a standard to maintain. |
| `03-resources/` | Reference material, no action attached. |
| `04-archive/` | Finished or dormant. |
| `memory/` | Claude's one-fact memory notes and their index. |
| `routines/` | Prompts that run on a schedule. |

Navigation starts at `02-areas/areas.md` and `03-resources/resources.md`.

## Conventions

- `lowercase-with-hyphens` for all paths. No spaces, no mixed case.
- `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md` for anything inherently dated.
- One topic per file. Split past roughly 25 KB.
- Attachments in a folder beside the note that owns them, sharing its slug.
- One fact, one home. A fact lives in one file, and other files link to it.
- Files state the current conclusion. History is `git log`.

## Working with it

`.claude/CLAUDE.md` holds the instructions for the AI assistant. Available commands:

| Command | Use |
|---------|-----|
| `/init` | Start of session: what is active, what is stale. |
| `/capture` | File something out of the inbox. |
| `/weekly-review` | The weekly hygiene pass. Do not skip this one. |
| `/archive-sweep` | Move finished work out of the way. |

New notes start from `note-templates/`.

## Maintenance

The weekly review is the whole system. A second brain does not fail because the structure is wrong; it
fails because nothing ever leaves. Run `/weekly-review` once a week and act on it.
